From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:06:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1269/3799] soh: rename D_8015FA94 -> sUnusedDebugValue

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the in-tree comment on its declaration reads "// no known symbols"; nothing reads or writes it.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_debug.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_debug.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_debug.c b/soh/src/code/z_debug.c
index 90a84c544..f158d3000 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_debug.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_debug.c
@@ -14,7 +14,8 @@ typedef struct {
 } InputCombo;
 
 GameInfo* gGameInfo;
-s32 D_8015FA94; // no known symbols
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was D_8015FA94: the in-tree comment on its declaration reads "// no known symbols"; nothing reads or writes it.
+s32 sUnusedDebugValue; // no known symbols, was D_8015FA94 [LLM:HIGH]
 PrintTextBuffer D_8015FA98[0x16];
 
 s16 D_8011E0B0 = 0; // PrintTextBuffer index
